// ---- Phase 5 batch C (R4): bangumi-data, a shipped library-scoped index (ui/vendor/bangumi-data/index.json, made by tools/bangumi-data-index.js
// from the pinned data.json; CC BY 4.0, named in the attribution text dsNoticeHtml). It maps provider ids to provider ids and nothing else:
//   - read only from ids the store already holds (the work's AniList / MAL (the cached entry's idMal) / Bangumi / TMDB link, a season's identity
//     as seasonIdentity reads it); never from a title. Lineage per target, the first anchor that is not the target itself: work AniList <- Bangumi,
//     TMDB; MAL <- AniList, Bangumi, TMDB; Bangumi <- AniList, MAL, TMDB; TMDB <- AniList, MAL, Bangumi (AniList is never derived from its own
//     idMal: one lineage); a season: AniList <- Bangumi, the TMDB season; Bangumi <- AniList, MAL, the TMDB season; TMDB <- AniList, MAL, Bangumi.
//   - one id on several entries (the 2012 series and its 2014 re-edit): the entry the record's other ids agree with, else none.
//   - kind gate (a film takes movie / ova entries, a series tv / web / ova); placement gate (O5, TMDB season numbers): a season anchor whose TMDB
