//              every comparison uses, drops punctuation, so 【推しの子】 equals the entry 【推しの子】).
//   variants   the search forms of the primary term (alTermVariants, the rule the terms always had): the search texts and the
//              negative-cache fingerprint (queryFp), unchanged for an unchanged term.
//   discovery  every other term: the variants that are not the primary itself, the .nfo <title> (item.raw.nfoTitle), the folder / file
//              title (parsed, then frozen) when it is not the primary, a film's own folder (D16). They find candidates; they never authorize
//              a write (the variants among them feed bgmBridge as the terms always did).
//   search     what alIdentify asks AniList with (one alSearchMany request, the first 6): the primary itself when no variant equals it,
